course: dictionary
lesson: 539
title: The Atlantic Ocean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The Atlantic Ocean is the second largest ocean in the world. It lies between the Americas on the west and Europe and Africa on the east.
explain: Atlantic with a capital A is the name of the ocean, like Paris or Mary. The Atlantic Ocean, the Atlantic coast and the North Atlantic are all names of places, so they start with capital letters.
explain: Atlantic can also be an adjective, a describing word, meaning to do with this ocean: «Atlantic salmon» and «the Atlantic coast». Ireland and the UK face the Atlantic on their west side.
fact: The Atlantic Ocean lies between North and South America on one side and Europe and Africa on the other.
fact: Sailors such as Columbus crossed the Atlantic in sailing ships.
fact: «Guglielmo Marconi sent radio signals across the Atlantic in 1901.»
fact: «The same kind of storm is called a hurricane in the Atlantic.»
fact: When you mean the ocean, write Atlantic with a capital A.
exercise: What is the Atlantic? | A small lake in the Alps | *The second largest ocean in the world, between the Americas and Europe and Africa | A mountain range in Africa
exercise: Which is written correctly? | atlantic ocean | atlantic Ocean | *Atlantic Ocean
exercise: What does «cross the Atlantic» mean? | To dig a hole in the sand | *To sail or fly from one side of the ocean to the other | To walk around a small pond
test: The Atlantic lies between the Americas and which two continents? | *Europe and Africa | Antarctica and Asia | Asia and Australia
test: In «Latitude says how far north or south of the Equator a place is, and longitude says how far east or west of Greenwich», what does longitude tell us? | *How far east or west of Greenwich a place is | How deep the ocean is | How many fish live there
exam: Which sentence uses the name of the ocean correctly? | *She crossed the Atlantic in a boat | she crossed the atlantic in a boat | She crossed the atlantic Ocean in a boat
